+// Rounds a preview and shrinks it to the card. The body is laid out at the
+// window's own size and scaled down as a whole, so the offscreen texture holds
+// the window at full resolution: one texel per window pixel. Shrinking that
+// with a single bilinear lookup skips most of the pixels at the scales Grid
+// uses (about half size on a wide display) and reads as blur and shimmer, so
+// each screen pixel averages a 4x4 grid of lookups spread across the area it
+// covers. At full size the lookups collapse onto one texel and the preview
+// matches the window exactly.
